<p>
  The Web UI reports through your <%= details[:type] %> <code>Karafka.producer</code>.
  If this producer hits a fatal error (for example, it gets fenced or runs into an idempotence
  sequence error), the Web UI stops receiving reports too, so you lose visibility right when
  your application has producer problems. If you want to keep them separate, you can configure a
  <a href="https://karafka.io/docs/Web-UI-Configuration/#using-a-custom-web-ui-producer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">custom Web UI producer</a>.
</p>
